WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.250
A dish: «le ceebu jën».

2
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.170
A greeting: «faire la bise»,

3
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.850
kisses on the cheeks.

4
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.490
A law: a 2016 French labor law
requires many companies to negotiate,

5
00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.480
or set rules on, «le
droit à la déconnexion»:

6
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.230
switching off from work
messages outside working hours.

7
00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:21.620
You can describe all
three in perfect French.

8
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.950
But does that show what
anyone actually cares about?

9
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.180
So how do you get from what people do

10
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.890
to what they value?

11
00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.900
In this mission, you'll sort products,

12
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.910
practices and perspectives on an iceberg.

13
00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.110
Then you'll build sentences in the lab,

14
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:39.860
chip by chip, and dodge the
traps hidden among them.

15
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:43.720
Your mission: find out how to
show what a culture values,

16
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.170
not just what it does.
